  "definition": "An asset pipeline is an automated, staged workflow that ingests raw digital content\u2014such as meshes, textures, audio, and animations\u2014and transforms it through processing, optimisation, and packaging steps into runtime-ready formats. It enforces consistency, enables version control, and reduces manual labour in content production. Asset pipelines are foundational to game development, visual effects, and metaverse platform engineering. They increasingly incorporate AI-assisted compression and level-of-detail generation to scale content delivery.",
